      "title": "原積分又出現",
      "prompt": "$\\int_0^1\\frac{\\ln(1+x)}{1+x^2}\\,dx$",
      "problemId": "world-015",
      "steps": [
        "$I(a)=\\int_0^1\\frac{\\ln(1+ax)}{1+x^2}\\,dx$，$I(0)=0$，原題是 $I(1)$。",
        "$I'(a)=\\int_0^1\\frac{x}{(1+ax)(1+x^2)}\\,dx$。部分分式：$\\frac{x}{(1+ax)(1+x^2)}=\\frac{1}{1+a^2}\\left[\\frac{x+a}{1+x^2}-\\frac{a}{1+ax}\\right]$，積分得 $I'(a)=\\frac{1}{1+a^2}\\left[\\frac{\\ln 2}{2}+\\frac{a\\pi}{4}-\\ln(1+a)\\right]$。",
        "從 $0$ 積到 $1$：$I(1)=\\frac{\\ln 2}{2}\\cdot\\frac{\\pi}{4}+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\cdot\\frac{\\ln 2}{2}-\\int_0^1\\frac{\\ln(1+a)}{1+a^2}\\,da$。（$\\int_0^1\\frac{da}{1+a^2}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$，$\\int_0^1\\frac{a\\,da}{1+a^2}=\\frac{\\ln 2}{2}$。）",
        "最後一項正是 $I(1)$ 本身：$I(1)=\\frac{\\pi\\ln 2}{4}-I(1)$，所以 $I(1)=\\frac{\\pi\\ln 2}{8}$。"
